G2D hardware framebuffer rotation for the A133 display driver.

Vendor patch (Dechuang IoT, 2025-10-11 "a133-tina-bsp-update", supplied for the
Zero 28 and the XU20) WITH the 90/270 fixes from acmeplus (gist
b2f9143b6e6f70d4150ae8372018ec46) folded in - they correct lines the vendor patch
itself adds, so they cannot be a separate patch here (one owner per line, or
apply-sdk-mods reads this one as unapplied and re-applies it forcibly).

It rotates the framebuffer with G2D on each flip, gated by
CONFIG_SUNXI_DISP2_FB_HW_ROTATION_SUPPORT and driven from the device tree
(disp_rotation_used, degree0); rotation forces the fb into double buffering. G2D
moves to subsys_initcall on our SoC - the SDK already does that for sun8iw11p1 -
so it is up before disp needs it, and Fb_copy_boot_fb rotates the framebuffer
U-Boot hands over.

The three folded fixes, all reachable only at 90/270 (the Zero 28's case):
  * fb_g2d_set_degree crossed the destination clip rectangle's width and height.
  * fb_g2d_rot_create validated the degree with && where || was meant.
  * Fb_copy_boot_fb did not swap the destination's width and height.

These boards present through fbdev (measured 2026-09-19 on the Zero 28: fb0's pan
offset alternates 0,0 <-> 0,640 while the UI runs, and dc_sunxi sits at refcount 0),
so this path carries everything on screen, not just the console.
